  "validity_note": "CoolProp's incompressible aqueous glycerol correlation (INCOMP::MGL), built on Melinder (2010). Tabulated for 10-60 wt% glycerol over -30 to 40 degC. Glycerol is a non-toxic, food- and pharma-grade non-electrolyte coolant, so it is modelled with CoolProp rather than the Laliberte electrolyte correlation; it is markedly more viscous than the glycols at the same strength, which matters for pump and pressure-drop work. Each cell sits above the solution's freezing line; cells below it are left blank and the explorer will not interpolate across them. Values are for preliminary design; verify against vendor data for critical service.",
